subject: forkd
Zero-to-first-fork in one command. Preflights the host, heals what's missing with your consent (guest kernel download, tap device, per-child netns), bakes a Python snapshot from Docker (or pulls one from the hub when Docker is absent), then forks N children and prints per-child timings.

Run as: sudo -E forkd quickstart

Usage: forkd quickstart [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -n, --n <N>
          How many children to fork for the demo
          
          [default: 10]

      --image <IMAGE>
          Docker image the parent snapshot is baked from. Ignored when Docker is unavailable (hub pull route)
          
          [default: python:3.12-slim]

  -y, --yes
          Answer yes to all setup prompts (kernel download, tap creation, netns provisioning) — for non-interactive use

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
